{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523719325,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f2e430001UyHpmIAYWCjcxv","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f2d72e001M9a2banpSyX8Si","type":"tool","id":"call_af2e2b2a80de415f893334e4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","limit":470,"offset":140},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 140-609\n140:     There is no direct-append exception. The run-now sentinels, the restored-sentinel row and\n141:     the synthesis reconciliation rows are canonical ledger events, because state_log is a\n142:     projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger and a row written beside it is dropped by\n143:     the next refresh.\n144: \n145: state_paths:\n146:   # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n147:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep root-local\n148:   # research/ and child phases keep local research/ packet directories.\n149:   packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n150:   config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json\"\n151:   state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n152:   status_ledger: \"{artifact_dir}/orchestration-status.log\"\n153:   strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n154:   registry: \"{artifact_dir}/findings-registry.json\"\n155:   dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-dashboard.md\"\n156:   pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-pause\"\n157:   run_now_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\"\n158:   lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research.lock\"\n159:   prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n160:   iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n161:   iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n162:   # Per-iteration structured delta stream (one file per iteration) — complement to the\n163:   # canonical state_log append. The delta file MUST contain at least one record whose\n164:   # `type === \"iteration\"` so the reducer can rehydrate iteration state after a partial\n165:   # run. Variants like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer; the\n166:   # post_dispatch_validate step enforces the canonical type below.\n167:   delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n168:   delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n169:   research_output: \"{artifact_dir}/research.md\"\n170:   resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n171:   archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n172:   synthesis_snapshot_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/synthesis-v{generation}.md\"\n173: \n174: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n175: # WORKFLOW\n176: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n177: workflow:\n178: \n179:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n180:     description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n181:     note: \"Root specs keep research artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/research/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/research/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/research_archive/{packet}/.\"\n182:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n183:     if_present:\n184:       bind:\n185:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n186:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n187:         artifact_subfolder: null\n188:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n189:     if_absent:\n190:       command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'research')));\\\"\"\n191:       outputs:\n192:         - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local research owner directory\"\n193:         - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n194:         - artifact_dir: \"Resolved research packet directory for this target\"\n195:         - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local research archive directory for this target\"\n196: \n197:   step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n198:     description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n199:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n200:     if_present:\n201:       bind:\n202:         reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n203:     if_absent:\n204:       bind:\n205:         reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n206: \n207:   step_fanout_spawn:\n208:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n209:     skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n210:     instructions: |\n211:       Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n212:       isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n213:       fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n214:       deep/research command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n215:       deep-research agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n216:       sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n217:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n218:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n219:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n220:     sub_steps:\n221:       step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n222:         description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n223:         skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n224:         command: |\n225:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n226:             --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n227:             --loop-type research \\\n228:             --research-topic \"{research_topic}\" \\\n229:             --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n230:             --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n231:             --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n232:             --stop-policy {stop_policy} \\\n233:             --convergence-mode {convergence_mode}\n234:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n235:         wait_for_completion: true\n236: \n237:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n238:   # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n239:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n240:   phase_init:\n241:     purpose: Create all state files for the research session\n242:     steps:\n243: \n244:       step_preflight_contract:\n245:         action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n246:         verify:\n247:           - required_values_present: [research_topic, spec_folder, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n248:           - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n249:           - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n250:           - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n251:         on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n252: \n253:       step_create_directories:\n254:         action: \"Create spec folder and research packet directories if they don't exist\"\n255:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n256: \n257:       step_detect_resource_map:\n258:         action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist the flag and seed Known Context\"\n259:         inspect:\n260:           - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n261:         classify:\n262:           present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n263:           absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n264:         outputs:\n265:           - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n266:           - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: summarize the map by section with entry counts across READMEs, Documents, Commands, Agents, Skills, Specs, Scripts, Tests, Config, and Meta, plus a one-line theme summary for each section. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n267: \n268:       step_resolve_canonical_names:\n269:         action: \"Resolve canonical research packet artifact names before classification\"\n270:         inspect_legacy:\n271:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/config.json\"\n272:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/state.jsonl\"\n273:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/strategy.md\"\n274:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dashboard.md\"\n275:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/.pause\"\n276:         migration_policy: \"dual-read / single-write for 4 weeks\"\n277:         on_legacy_read:\n278:           set: { legacy_migration_detected: true, migration_recorded: false }\n279:           outputs:\n280:             - legacy_path: \"The legacy artifact path that was read\"\n281:             - canonical_path: \"The canonical artifact path it maps to\"\n282:           note: \"Only detect and bind here. The migration row is appended by step_record_artifact_migration, once the session is classified and the run is open, because an append before classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one.\"\n283: \n284:       step_acquire_lock:\n285:         action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n286:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms 1800000\"\n287:         on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed: another deep-research run already holds this packet.\"\n288:         note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n289:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n290:         # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n291:         on_halt:\n292:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n293:           applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\", \"step_preinit_spec_branch.conflict-detected\"]\n294:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n295:         on_cancel:\n296:           action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n297:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n298:         on_workflow_exit:\n299:           action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n300:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent, safe to invoke when already released\"\n301: \n302:       step_classify_session:\n303:         action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n304:         inspect:\n305:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n306:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n307:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n308:         classify:\n309:           fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n310:           resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and agree on topic/spec folder; missing wait-checkpoint fields are read as nextRunAt:null and remainingDelayMs:null\"\n311:           completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n312:           invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n313:         outputs:\n314:           - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n315:         on_resume:\n316:           # Resume is a WRITE-PATH. Produces `iteration-NNN.md` + JSONL appends.\n317:           # Gate 3 lists it as a trigger beside save context, save memory and /speckit:save.\n318:           gate3_classification: write-path\n319:           gate3_rationale: \"resume produces iteration-NNN.md writes and JSONL state-log appends\"\n320:           log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n321:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"resumed\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"resume\",\"continuedFromRun\":{iteration_count},\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":null,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n322:           skip_to: phase_loop\n323:         on_restart:\n324:           action: \"Archive the current research packet under the root-level research_archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n325:           command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n326:           set:\n327:             lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n328:             parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n329:             generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n330:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"restarted\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"restart\",\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n331:           skip_to: step_create_config\n332:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract for the one-session contract.\"\n333:         on_completed_session:\n334:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Do not route directly to synthesis; archive the completed research/ tree or start a fresh packet instead.\"\n335:           halt: true\n336:           message: \"Completed deep-research packet detected. Archive or replace the existing research/ tree before starting a new session.\"\n337:         on_invalid_state:\n338:           halt: true\n339:           message: \"Existing deep-research state is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid research packet before continuing.\"\n340:         on_fresh:\n341:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n342: \n343:       step_resolve_session_id:\n344:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve the auto-generated fallback\"\n345:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n346:         if_present:\n347:           bind:\n348:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n349:         if_absent:\n350:           bind:\n351:             # The token is bound here so the fallback literal resolves to a real timestamp when no caller session_id is supplied.\n352:             AUTO_SESSION_ID: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n353:             session_id_init: \"{AUTO_SESSION_ID}\"\n354: \n355:       step_create_config:\n356:         action: \"Create deep-research-config.json from template\"\n357:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json\n358:         populate:\n359:           topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n360:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n361:           minIterations: 3\n362:           # Semantic: newInfoRatio with negative-knowledge emphasis. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n363:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n364:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n365:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n366:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n367:           stuckThreshold: 3\n368:           minIdeaObservations: 2\n369:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n370:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n371:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n372:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-research.md:73 (default true; false when flag is set).\n373:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n374:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n375:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n376:           status: \"initialized\"\n377:           executionMode: \"auto\"\n378:           lineage.sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n379:           lineage.parentSessionId: null\n380:           lineage.lineageMode: \"new\"\n381:           lineage.generation: 1\n382:           lineage.continuedFromRun: null\n383:           nextRunAt: null\n384:           remainingDelayMs: null\n385:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n386: \n387:       step_create_state_log:\n388:         action: \"Open the research run by appending deep_research.run_initialized through the gateway\"\n389:         note: |\n390:           The state log is a projection rebuilt by the gateway. Recording the run's opening in\n391:           the ledger gives every later state append the same authorized, ordered source.\n392:         command: |\n393:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n394:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n395:           EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n396:           node -e '\n397:             const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n398:             const [configPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n399:             const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n400:             const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n401:             const sha = (value) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(value).digest(\"hex\");\n402:             const lineage = config.lineage || {};\n403:             const sessionId = lineage.sessionId;\n404:             const lineageId = lineage.parentSessionId || sessionId;\n405:             const generation = Number(lineage.generation) || 1;\n406:             const configDigest = sha(raw);\n407:             // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n408:             // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n409:             const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n410:               ? config.topic\n411:               : null;\n412:             const event = {\n413:               stem: \"deep_research.run_initialized\",\n414:               scope: { runId: sessionId, lineageId },\n415:               data: {\n416:                 generation,\n417:                 ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n418:                 charterDigest: sha(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify({\n419:                   topic: config.topic,\n420:                   specFolder: config.specFolder || \"\",\n421:                 }))),\n422:                 configDigest,\n423:                 executorFingerprint: sha(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(config.executor || {}))),\n424:                 replayFingerprint: sha(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify({\n425:                   runId: sessionId,\n426:                   lineageId,\n427:                   generation,\n428:                   configDigest,\n429:                 }))),\n430:                 maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n431:                 convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + (\n432:                   (config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"\n433:                 ),\n434:               },\n435:             };\n436:             process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(event));\n437:           ' \"{state_paths.config}\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n438:           node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode research --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n439:           STATUS=$?\n440:           rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n441:           exit \"$STATUS\"\n442:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n443: \n444:       step_create_strategy:\n445:         action: \"Create strategy file from template with initial questions\"\n446:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\n447:         populate:\n448:           topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n449:           key_questions: \"Derive 3-5 key questions from the research topic\"\n450:           known_context: \"None\"\n451:           known_context_summary: \"None\"\n452:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n453:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n454:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n455: \n456:       step_create_registry:\n457:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned findings registry\"\n458:         content: '{\"openQuestions\":[],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}'\n459:         output: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n460: \n461:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n462:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n463:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n464:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n465:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n466: \n467:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n468:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n469:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n470:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n471: \n472:       step_detect_spec_present:\n473:         action: \"Classify late-INIT spec.md state after the durable research packet exists\"\n474:         inspect:\n475:           - \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n476:           - \"{state_paths.lock_file}\"\n477:         classify:\n478:           no-spec: \"spec.md is absent before any pre-init mutation\"\n479:           spec-present: \"spec.md exists and approved host anchors are available for bounded mutation\"\n480:           spec-just-created-by-this-run: \"spec.md already carries this run's DR seed markers and should not be reseeded\"\n481:           conflict-detected: \"missing host anchor, duplicate markers, or generated-block ambiguity makes mutation unsafe\"\n482:         outputs:\n483:           - folder_state: \"no-spec | spec-present | spec-just-created-by-this-run | conflict-detected\"\n484:           - normalized_topic: \"Trim, lowercase, and collapse whitespace in research_topic before dedupe checks\"\n485:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"spec_check_result\",\"folder_state\":\"{folder_state}\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"lockPath\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n486: \n487:       step_preinit_spec_branch:\n488:         action: \"Run the bounded pre-init spec branch required by spec_check_protocol\"\n489:         protocol_reference: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\"\n490:         branches:\n491:           no-spec:\n492:             create: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n493:             seed_markers:\n494:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n495:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n496:             requirements_host: \"Seed Requirements from the research ask without broadening scope\"\n497:             scope_host: \"Seed Scope from the research ask without inventing implementation details\"\n498:             set:\n499:               folder_state: \"spec-just-created-by-this-run\"\n500:               validate_spec_doc: true\n501:             append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_seed_created\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-just-created-by-this-run\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Requirements\",\"Scope\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Seeded Level 1 spec.md from research topic with DR seed markers.\",\"seed_markers\":[\"DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS\",\"DR-SEED:SCOPE\"],\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n502:           spec-present:\n503:             edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n504:             set:\n505:               validate_spec_doc: true\n506:             idempotency_check:\n507:               host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n508:               normalized_match: \"Normalize the existing anchor text by lowercasing, stripping punctuation, collapsing whitespace, and trimming before comparing with {normalized_topic}.\"\n509:               if_match:\n510:                 skip_append: true\n511:                 append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_deduped\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Skipped duplicate pre-init topic append because normalized topic already exists in Open Questions.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n512:               if_no_match:\n513:                 append_only:\n514:                   - host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n515:                     content: \"Add the normalized research topic only if it is not already present.\"\n516:                   - host_anchor: \"Research Context\"\n517:                     content: \"Add a bounded note that deep-research is active for this topic and that research/research.md remains canonical.\"\n518:                 append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_added\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\",\"Research Context\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Appended bounded pre-init research context for the normalized topic.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n519:           spec-just-created-by-this-run:\n520:             verify_markers:\n521:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n522:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n523:             set:\n524:               validate_spec_doc: false\n525:             note: \"Treat already-seeded spec.md as a no-op guard and continue.\"\n526:           conflict-detected:\n527:             append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Pre-init spec.md mutation is ambiguous or unsafe.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n528:             halt: true\n529: \n530:       step_validate_preinit_spec_doc:\n531:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after any deep-research pre-init spec.md mutation\"\n532:         condition: \"validate_spec_doc\"\n533:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n534:         note: \"This enforces the authored-spec markdown structural contract without applying full-packet required-file or completeness checks to workflow-owned research artifacts. It uses the Node validation orchestrator, whose strict path was measured at about 108ms for a fresh Level 3 packet on the local harness.\"\n535: \n536:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_started:\n537:         action: \"Emit a single-loop started row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n538:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n539:         canonical_lifecycle_event: \"iteration_start\"\n540:         command: |\n541:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n542:           import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n543: \n544:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n545:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n546: \n547:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n548:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n549:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n550:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{AUTO_SESSION_ID}');\n551:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? 1);\n552:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n553:           const row = {\n554:             event: 'started',\n555:             label: 'single',\n556:             at: timestamp,\n557:             duration_ms: 0,\n558:             loop_type: 'research',\n559:             sessionId,\n560:             generation,\n561:             gauges: { iterations: 0, elapsed_ms: 0, score: 0 },\n562:           };\n563: \n564:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n565:             diffData: { event: row.event, label: row.label, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: 0, score: 0 } },\n566:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n567:           });\n568:           if (appended) {\n569:             try {\n570:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n571:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n572:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n573:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation },\n574:                 event: row.event,\n575:                 status: 'running',\n576:               });\n577:             } catch {}\n578:           }\n579:           EOF\n580:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n581:         outputs:\n582:           - status_ledger_started: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event started\"\n583: \n584:       step_init_complete:\n585:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created.\"\n586:         set: { current_iteration: 1, current_segment: 1, stuck_count: 0 }\n587: \n588:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n589:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n590:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n591:   phase_loop:\n592:     purpose: Dispatch agent iterations until convergence\n593:     repeat: true\n594:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n595:     steps:\n596: \n597:       step_refresh_lock:\n598:         action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat before the iteration begins\"\n599:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n600:         on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet and must stop rather than iterate without it.\"\n601: \n602:       step_record_artifact_migration:\n603:         action: \"Record a legacy artifact alias read once per session, after the run is open\"\n604:         skip_when: \"legacy_migration_detected != true or migration_recorded == true\"\n605:         append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"migration\",\"legacyPath\":\"{legacy_path}\",\"canonicalPath\":\"{canonical_path}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n606:         set: { migration_recorded: true }\n607: \n608:       step_read_state:\n609:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL and strategy\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 610]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 140-609\n140:     There is no direct-append exception. The run-now sentinels, the restored-sentinel row and\n141:     the synthesis reconciliation rows are canonical ledger events, because state_log is a\n142:     projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger and a row written beside it is dropped by\n143:     the next refresh.\n144: \n145: state_paths:\n146:   # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n147:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep root-local\n148:   # research/ and child phases keep local research/ packet directories.\n149:   packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n150:   config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json\"\n151:   state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n152:   status_ledger: \"{artifact_dir}/orchestration-status.log\"\n153:   strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n154:   registry: \"{artifact_dir}/findings-registry.json\"\n155:   dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-dashboard.md\"\n156:   pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-pause\"\n157:   run_now_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\"\n158:   lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research.lock\"\n159:   prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n160:   iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n161:   iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n162:   # Per-iteration structured delta stream (one file per iteration) — complement to the\n163:   # canonical state_log append. The delta file MUST contain at least one record whose\n164:   # `type === \"iteration\"` so the reducer can rehydrate iteration state after a partial\n165:   # run. Variants like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer; the\n166:   # post_dispatch_validate step enforces the canonical type below.\n167:   delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n168:   delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n169:   research_output: \"{artifact_dir}/research.md\"\n170:   resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n171:   archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n172:   synthesis_snapshot_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/synthesis-v{generation}.md\"\n173: \n174: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n175: # WORKFLOW\n176: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n177: workflow:\n178: \n179:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n180:     description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n181:     note: \"Root specs keep research artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/research/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/research/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/research_archive/{packet}/.\"\n182:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n183:     if_present:\n184:       bind:\n185:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n186:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n187:         artifact_subfolder: null\n188:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n189:     if_absent:\n190:       command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'research')));\\\"\"\n191:       outputs:\n192:         - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local research owner directory\"\n193:         - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n194:         - artifact_dir: \"Resolved research packet directory for this target\"\n195:         - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local research archive directory for this target\"\n196: \n197:   step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n198:     description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n199:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n200:     if_present:\n201:       bind:\n202:         reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n203:     if_absent:\n204:       bind:\n205:         reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n206: \n207:   step_fanout_spawn:\n208:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n209:     skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n210:     instructions: |\n211:       Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n212:       isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n213:       fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n214:       deep/research command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n215:       deep-research agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n216:       sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n217:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n218:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n219:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n220:     sub_steps:\n221:       step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n222:         description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n223:         skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n224:         command: |\n225:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n226:             --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n227:             --loop-type research \\\n228:             --research-topic \"{research_topic}\" \\\n229:             --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n230:             --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n231:             --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n232:             --stop-policy {stop_policy} \\\n233:             --convergence-mode {convergence_mode}\n234:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n235:         wait_for_completion: true\n236: \n237:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n238:   # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n239:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n240:   phase_init:\n241:     purpose: Create all state files for the research session\n242:     steps:\n243: \n244:       step_preflight_contract:\n245:         action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n246:         verify:\n247:           - required_values_present: [research_topic, spec_folder, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n248:           - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n249:           - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n250:           - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n251:         on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n252: \n253:       step_create_directories:\n254:         action: \"Create spec folder and research packet directories if they don't exist\"\n255:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n256: \n257:       step_detect_resource_map:\n258:         action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist the flag and seed Known Context\"\n259:         inspect:\n260:           - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n261:         classify:\n262:           present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n263:           absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n264:         outputs:\n265:           - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n266:           - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: summarize the map by section with entry counts across READMEs, Documents, Commands, Agents, Skills, Specs, Scripts, Tests, Config, and Meta, plus a one-line theme summary for each section. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n267: \n268:       step_resolve_canonical_names:\n269:         action: \"Resolve canonical research packet artifact names before classification\"\n270:         inspect_legacy:\n271:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/config.json\"\n272:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/state.jsonl\"\n273:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/strategy.md\"\n274:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dashboard.md\"\n275:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/.pause\"\n276:         migration_policy: \"dual-read / single-write for 4 weeks\"\n277:         on_legacy_read:\n278:           set: { legacy_migration_detected: true, migration_recorded: false }\n279:           outputs:\n280:             - legacy_path: \"The legacy artifact path that was read\"\n281:             - canonical_path: \"The canonical artifact path it maps to\"\n282:           note: \"Only detect and bind here. The migration row is appended by step_record_artifact_migration, once the session is classified and the run is open, because an append before classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one.\"\n283: \n284:       step_acquire_lock:\n285:         action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n286:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms 1800000\"\n287:         on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed: another deep-research run already holds this packet.\"\n288:         note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n289:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n290:         # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n291:         on_halt:\n292:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n293:           applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\", \"step_preinit_spec_branch.conflict-detected\"]\n294:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n295:         on_cancel:\n296:           action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n297:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n298:         on_workflow_exit:\n299:           action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n300:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent, safe to invoke when already released\"\n301: \n302:       step_classify_session:\n303:         action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n304:         inspect:\n305:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n306:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n307:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n308:         classify:\n309:           fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n310:           resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and agree on topic/spec folder; missing wait-checkpoint fields are read as nextRunAt:null and remainingDelayMs:null\"\n311:           completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n312:           invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n313:         outputs:\n314:           - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n315:         on_resume:\n316:           # Resume is a WRITE-PATH. Produces `iteration-NNN.md` + JSONL appends.\n317:           # Gate 3 lists it as a trigger beside save context, save memory and /speckit:save.\n318:           gate3_classification: write-path\n319:           gate3_rationale: \"resume produces iteration-NNN.md writes and JSONL state-log appends\"\n320:           log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n321:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"resumed\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"resume\",\"continuedFromRun\":{iteration_count},\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":null,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n322:           skip_to: phase_loop\n323:         on_restart:\n324:           action: \"Archive the current research packet under the root-level research_archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n325:           command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n326:           set:\n327:             lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n328:             parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n329:             generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n330:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"restarted\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"restart\",\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n331:           skip_to: step_create_config\n332:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract for the one-session contract.\"\n333:         on_completed_session:\n334:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Do not route directly to synthesis; archive the completed research/ tree or start a fresh packet instead.\"\n335:           halt: true\n336:           message: \"Completed deep-research packet detected. Archive or replace the existing research/ tree before starting a new session.\"\n337:         on_invalid_state:\n338:           halt: true\n339:           message: \"Existing deep-research state is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid research packet before continuing.\"\n340:         on_fresh:\n341:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n342: \n343:       step_resolve_session_id:\n344:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve the auto-generated fallback\"\n345:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n346:         if_present:\n347:           bind:\n348:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n349:         if_absent:\n350:           bind:\n351:             # The token is bound here so the fallback literal resolves to a real timestamp when no caller session_id is supplied.\n352:             AUTO_SESSION_ID: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n353:             session_id_init: \"{AUTO_SESSION_ID}\"\n354: \n355:       step_create_config:\n356:         action: \"Create deep-research-config.json from template\"\n357:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json\n358:         populate:\n359:           topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n360:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n361:           minIterations: 3\n362:           # Semantic: newInfoRatio with negative-knowledge emphasis. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n363:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n364:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n365:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n366:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n367:           stuckThreshold: 3\n368:           minIdeaObservations: 2\n369:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n370:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n371:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n372:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-research.md:73 (default true; false when flag is set).\n373:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n374:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n375:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n376:           status: \"initialized\"\n377:           executionMode: \"auto\"\n378:           lineage.sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n379:           lineage.parentSessionId: null\n380:           lineage.lineageMode: \"new\"\n381:           lineage.generation: 1\n382:           lineage.continuedFromRun: null\n383:           nextRunAt: null\n384:           remainingDelayMs: null\n385:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n386: \n387:       step_create_state_log:\n388:         action: \"Open the research run by appending deep_research.run_initialized through the gateway\"\n389:         note: |\n390:           The state log is a projection rebuilt by the gateway. Recording the run's opening in\n391:           the ledger gives every later state append the same authorized, ordered source.\n392:         command: |\n393:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n394:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n395:           EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n396:           node -e '\n397:             const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n398:             const [configPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n399:             const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n400:             const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n401:             const sha = (value) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(value).digest(\"hex\");\n402:             const lineage = config.lineage || {};\n403:             const sessionId = lineage.sessionId;\n404:             const lineageId = lineage.parentSessionId || sessionId;\n405:             const generation = Number(lineage.generation) || 1;\n406:             const configDigest = sha(raw);\n407:             // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n408:             // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n409:             const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n410:               ? config.topic\n411:               : null;\n412:             const event = {\n413:               stem: \"deep_research.run_initialized\",\n414:               scope: { runId: sessionId, lineageId },\n415:               data: {\n416:                 generation,\n417:                 ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n418:                 charterDigest: sha(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify({\n419:                   topic: config.topic,\n420:                   specFolder: config.specFolder || \"\",\n421:                 }))),\n422:                 configDigest,\n423:                 executorFingerprint: sha(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(config.executor || {}))),\n424:                 replayFingerprint: sha(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify({\n425:                   runId: sessionId,\n426:                   lineageId,\n427:                   generation,\n428:                   configDigest,\n429:                 }))),\n430:                 maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n431:                 convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + (\n432:                   (config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"\n433:                 ),\n434:               },\n435:             };\n436:             process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(event));\n437:           ' \"{state_paths.config}\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n438:           node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode research --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n439:           STATUS=$?\n440:           rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n441:           exit \"$STATUS\"\n442:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n443: \n444:       step_create_strategy:\n445:         action: \"Create strategy file from template with initial questions\"\n446:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\n447:         populate:\n448:           topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n449:           key_questions: \"Derive 3-5 key questions from the research topic\"\n450:           known_context: \"None\"\n451:           known_context_summary: \"None\"\n452:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n453:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n454:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n455: \n456:       step_create_registry:\n457:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned findings registry\"\n458:         content: '{\"openQuestions\":[],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}'\n459:         output: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n460: \n461:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n462:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n463:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n464:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n465:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n466: \n467:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n468:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n469:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n470:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n471: \n472:       step_detect_spec_present:\n473:         action: \"Classify late-INIT spec.md state after the durable research packet exists\"\n474:         inspect:\n475:           - \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n476:           - \"{state_paths.lock_file}\"\n477:         classify:\n478:           no-spec: \"spec.md is absent before any pre-init mutation\"\n479:           spec-present: \"spec.md exists and approved host anchors are available for bounded mutation\"\n480:           spec-just-created-by-this-run: \"spec.md already carries this run's DR seed markers and should not be reseeded\"\n481:           conflict-detected: \"missing host anchor, duplicate markers, or generated-block ambiguity makes mutation unsafe\"\n482:         outputs:\n483:           - folder_state: \"no-spec | spec-present | spec-just-created-by-this-run | conflict-detected\"\n484:           - normalized_topic: \"Trim, lowercase, and collapse whitespace in research_topic before dedupe checks\"\n485:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"spec_check_result\",\"folder_state\":\"{folder_state}\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"lockPath\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n486: \n487:       step_preinit_spec_branch:\n488:         action: \"Run the bounded pre-init spec branch required by spec_check_protocol\"\n489:         protocol_reference: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\"\n490:         branches:\n491:           no-spec:\n492:             create: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n493:             seed_markers:\n494:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n495:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n496:             requirements_host: \"Seed Requirements from the research ask without broadening scope\"\n497:             scope_host: \"Seed Scope from the research ask without inventing implementation details\"\n498:             set:\n499:               folder_state: \"spec-just-created-by-this-run\"\n500:               validate_spec_doc: true\n501:             append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_seed_created\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-just-created-by-this-run\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Requirements\",\"Scope\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Seeded Level 1 spec.md from research topic with DR seed markers.\",\"seed_markers\":[\"DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS\",\"DR-SEED:SCOPE\"],\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n502:           spec-present:\n503:             edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n504:             set:\n505:               validate_spec_doc: true\n506:             idempotency_check:\n507:               host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n508:               normalized_match: \"Normalize the existing anchor text by lowercasing, stripping punctuation, collapsing whitespace, and trimming before comparing with {normalized_topic}.\"\n509:               if_match:\n510:                 skip_append: true\n511:                 append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_deduped\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Skipped duplicate pre-init topic append because normalized topic already exists in Open Questions.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n512:               if_no_match:\n513:                 append_only:\n514:                   - host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n515:                     content: \"Add the normalized research topic only if it is not already present.\"\n516:                   - host_anchor: \"Research Context\"\n517:                     content: \"Add a bounded note that deep-research is active for this topic and that research/research.md remains canonical.\"\n518:                 append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_added\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\",\"Research Context\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Appended bounded pre-init research context for the normalized topic.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n519:           spec-just-created-by-this-run:\n520:             verify_markers:\n521:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n522:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n523:             set:\n524:               validate_spec_doc: false\n525:             note: \"Treat already-seeded spec.md as a no-op guard and continue.\"\n526:           conflict-detected:\n527:             append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Pre-init spec.md mutation is ambiguous or unsafe.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n528:             halt: true\n529: \n530:       step_validate_preinit_spec_doc:\n531:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after any deep-research pre-init spec.md mutation\"\n532:         condition: \"validate_spec_doc\"\n533:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n534:         note: \"This enforces the authored-spec markdown structural contract without applying full-packet required-file or completeness checks to workflow-owned research artifacts. It uses the Node validation orchestrator, whose strict path was measured at about 108ms for a fresh Level 3 packet on the local harness.\"\n535: \n536:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_started:\n537:         action: \"Emit a single-loop started row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n538:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n539:         canonical_lifecycle_event: \"iteration_start\"\n540:         command: |\n541:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n542:           import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n543: \n544:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n545:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n546: \n547:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n548:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n549:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n550:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{AUTO_SESSION_ID}');\n551:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? 1);\n552:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n553:           const row = {\n554:             event: 'started',\n555:             label: 'single',\n556:             at: timestamp,\n557:             duration_ms: 0,\n558:             loop_type: 'research',\n559:             sessionId,\n560:             generation,\n561:             gauges: { iterations: 0, elapsed_ms: 0, score: 0 },\n562:           };\n563: \n564:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n565:             diffData: { event: row.event, label: row.label, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: 0, score: 0 } },\n566:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n567:           });\n568:           if (appended) {\n569:             try {\n570:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n571:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n572:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n573:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation },\n574:                 event: row.event,\n575:                 status: 'running',\n576:               });\n577:             } catch {}\n578:           }\n579:           EOF\n580:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n581:         outputs:\n582:           - status_ledger_started: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event started\"\n583: \n584:       step_init_complete:\n585:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created.\"\n586:         set: { current_iteration: 1, current_segment: 1, stuck_count: 0 }\n587: \n588:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n589:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n590:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n591:   phase_loop:\n592:     purpose: Dispatch agent iterations until convergence\n593:     repeat: true\n594:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n595:     steps:\n596: \n597:       step_refresh_lock:\n598:         action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat before the iteration begins\"\n599:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n600:         on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet and must stop rather than iterate without it.\"\n601: \n602:       step_record_artifact_migration:\n603:         action: \"Record a legacy artifact alias read once per session, after the run is open\"\n604:         skip_when: \"legacy_migration_detected != true or migration_recorded == true\"\n605:         append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"migration\",\"legacyPath\":\"{legacy_path}\",\"canonicalPath\":\"{canonical_path}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n606:         set: { migration_recorded: true }\n607: \n608:       step_read_state:\n609:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL and strategy\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 610]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\",\"limit\":470,\"offset\":140}"},"time":{"start":1794523718704,"end":1794523719325}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794523720413,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f2eadd0010n2Hw41chsJkSJ","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f2d72e001M9a2banpSyX8Si","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"5e9f74d4d7bc39b26660156773ec599c77c4ac09","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":2004,"output":83,"reasoning":116,"cache":{"read":41216,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794523726820,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f303e4001j4VYeVPcFoARfZ","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f2eae1001KkMTVwaKv4llDi","type":"step-start","snapshot":"5e9f74d4d7bc39b26660156773ec599c77c4ac09"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523728841,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f30b05001Ub4FsWgFmNCv9H","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f2eae1001KkMTVwaKv4llDi","type":"tool","id":"call_e8c311ba61f8489081219f7d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523728645,"end":1794523728841}}}}
