{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523936266,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f5fe8800135FNDoWWB5ZkNO","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f5eeba0017dEdBN1d2E3lmL","type":"tool","id":"call_63fc8f5cbd01402c9a9b6d84","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli command surfacing\ndescription: Cross-CLI usefulness angle for command surfacing after planned phases 005-008.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nEstablish, per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), whether a model starts an advisor-offered command, what stops it, and which post-005-008 change raises the start rate for the least work.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Reads evidence from the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`) and the pre-arm behaviour log.\n- Writes only inside the lineage directory.\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nCross-CLI command surfacing after planned phases 005-008: per-runtime evidence of whether a model starts an offered advisor command, what stops it, and which fix raises start rate.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\n- [ ] Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\n- [ ] Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\n- [ ] How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\n- [ ] What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending what phases 005-008 already plan.\n- Implementing any fix (research only).\n- The UX and performance angles owned by sibling lineages, except where they change per-runtime start behaviour.\n- Re-running pi, starting or stopping ollama, or running the full vitest suite.\n- Reading or printing holdout-split rows from command-prompts.jsonl.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Max 5 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\n- No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[Populated after iteration 1]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[Populated after iteration 1]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach is tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Populated from iteration dead ends]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nIteration 1: score runs-pre.jsonl and map, per runtime, which hook/pointer surface exists today and which of the planned 005-008 mechanisms is supposed to serve it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nEvidence pointers (read-only):\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`, `decision-record.md`, `goal.md`.\n- Child plans/tasks: `005-recommendation-contract-and-brief`, `006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers`, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof`, `008-embedder-setup-and-cost`.\n- `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl` scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` (baseline: claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7; COMMAND line 0 everywhere).\n- `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt` (skill.md shadows sibling commands as one Skill entry on Claude Code).\n- `008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt` and `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`.\n- Runtime hook/pointer surfaces under `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.opencode/`, `.pi/`, `.devin/`, `.dsh/`, and the advisor runtime `runtime/` tree.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: advisor hook, brief renderer, gate-2 binding, runtime pointer installers.\n- Reuse candidates: existing scorer `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, existing hooks.\n- Integration points: hook brief text, command file layout, per-runtime config.\n- Constraints: planned-not-built phases, read-only git, no pi/ollama.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-12T22:50:26.300Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli command surfacing\\ndescription: Cross-CLI usefulness angle for command surfacing after planned phases 005-008.\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nEstablish, per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), whether a model starts an advisor-offered command, what stops it, and which post-005-008 change raises the start rate for the least work.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Reads evidence from the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`) and the pre-arm behaviour log.\\n- Writes only inside the lineage directory.\\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\\n\\n### Question Injection Surface\\n\\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nCross-CLI command surfacing after planned phases 005-008: per-runtime evidence of whether a model starts an offered advisor command, what stops it, and which fix raises start rate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\\n- [ ] Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\\n- [ ] Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\\n- [ ] How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\\n- [ ] What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending what phases 005-008 already plan.\\n- Implementing any fix (research only).\\n- The UX and performance angles owned by sibling lineages, except where they change per-runtime start behaviour.\\n- Re-running pi, starting or stopping ollama, or running the full vitest suite.\\n- Reading or printing holdout-split rows from command-prompts.jsonl.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Max 5 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\\n- No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[Populated after iteration 1]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[Populated after iteration 1]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach is tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Populated from iteration dead ends]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nIteration 1: score runs-pre.jsonl and map, per runtime, which hook/pointer surface exists today and which of the planned 005-008 mechanisms is supposed to serve it.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nEvidence pointers (read-only):\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`, `decision-record.md`, `goal.md`.\\n- Child plans/tasks: `005-recommendation-contract-and-brief`, `006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers`, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof`, `008-embedder-setup-and-cost`.\\n- `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl` scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` (baseline: claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7; COMMAND line 0 everywhere).\\n- `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt` (skill.md shadows sibling commands as one Skill entry on Claude Code).\\n- `008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt` and `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`.\\n- Runtime hook/pointer surfaces under `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.opencode/`, `.pi/`, `.devin/`, `.dsh/`, and the advisor runtime `runtime/` tree.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: advisor hook, brief renderer, gate-2 binding, runtime pointer installers.\\n- Reuse candidates: existing scorer `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, existing hooks.\\n- Integration points: hook brief text, command file layout, per-runtime config.\\n- Constraints: planned-not-built phases, read-only git, no pi/ollama.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 5\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-12T22:50:26.300Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523922056,"end":1794523936266}}}}
