{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524051835,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f7f2b5002K99LZzMeYdN9pd","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f7e418001suNztpdue2yPEt","type":"tool","id":"call_8251e3814c164d7b96d3a271","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"Advisor: \\|advisorBrief\\|renderAdvisorBrief\\|skill-advisor\" .skilled/hooks .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"--- claude UserPromptSubmit\"; node -e \"\nconst s=require('./.claude/settings.json');\nfor (const [ev,arr] of Object.entries(s.hooks||{})) {\n  console.log('EVENT',ev);\n  for (const m of arr) for (const h of (m.hooks||[])) console.log('  ',String(h.command).slice(0,160));\n}\" 2>&1 | head -50","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/claude/README.md:19:The canonical adapter lives in `system-skill-advisor` and calls `advanceDirectiveLifecycleBoundary` against the file-backed store. The Spec-Kit bridge shim resolves that compiled target and spawns it. Edit the targets, not the links.\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/claude/README.md:27:| `directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts` | Symlink to [`../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts`](../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts) | Link only. The target reads bounded stdin JSON with `session_id` and `boundary`, checks the kill switch and advances the store's session epoch, or its generation when identity is missing. | Fails open. A missing identity or a store failure advances nothing and returns false. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/claude/README.md:35:- [`../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts`](../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts): the canonical adapter.\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:24:The real code lives in `system-skill-advisor` (the canonical boundary adapter and the `lib/` decision + store) and `system-spec-kit` (a bridge shim that spawns the canonical target). This folder holds relative symlinks into both, indexed by runtime.\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:59:| **OpenCode** | — | — | `by-design`: embedded in `system-skill-advisor` lifecycle state (the OpenCode plugin) |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:72:    +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts        # symlink -> system-skill-advisor canonical boundary adapter\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:82:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts` | Canonical boundary adapter. Reads a bounded stdin JSON (`session_id`, `boundary`), checks the kill-switch, and calls `advanceDirectiveLifecycleBoundary` against the default file-backed store. Emits no model-visible output. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:84:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | The decision core: `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` (full vs suppressed), `advanceDirectiveLifecycleBoundary`, the `InMemoryDirectiveLifecycleStore`, and the default file-backed store handle. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:85:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle-contract.ts` | Constants and types: `DIRECTIVE_SEPARATOR` (`\\nDirectives:`), `MAX_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_SESSIONS` (64), `DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_SCHEMA_VERSION` (2), `DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DEDUP_ENV`. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:86:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts` | The cross-process durable file-backed store the default handle wraps. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:116:| Imports | Adapters import Node builtins only, plus the canonical `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts`, imported by its compiled `.js` name and the shared `hook-flags.cjs` resolver via `createRequire`. Nothing outside the repo. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:117:| Real code | Stays in `system-skill-advisor` and `system-spec-kit`; the hub entries are relative symlinks. |\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:126:npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:134:npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:143:  node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.js\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:154:- [`../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`](../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md): the advisor hook contract whose brief this concern dedups.\n.skilled/hooks/directive-lifecycle/README.md:155:- [`../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/`](../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/): the decision core, contract, and file-backed store.\n.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:47:# SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1         # skill-advisor brief on your prompts\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:11:import promptAdvisor from '../../../skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor';\n.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.test.ts:71:function registerInjectedInput(api: ExtensionAPI, suffix = 'Advisor: injected cli-devin example') {\n--- claude UserPromptSubmit\nEVENT PreToolUse\n   bash -c 'cd \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\" && node .skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs || { printf \"%s\\n\" \"mk-hook-drift host=claude event\n   bash -c 'cd \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\" && node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/claude/spec-gate-enforce.mjs || { printf \"%s\\n\" \"mk-hook-drift h\n   bash -c 'cd \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD