{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524103785,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f8bd59001R5r0IjuH0A6BFM","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f8a1f10014vTXIfSfzNkIHQ","type":"tool","id":"call_e4e113ee5c6545b297d3db5e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"diff <(node -e \"console.log(JSON.stringify(require('./.claude/settings.json')).length)\") /dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1; A=/private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/pre-claude; diff -q .claude/settings.json \"$A/.claude/settings.json\"; diff -q .codex/hooks.json \"$A/.codex/hooks.json\"; diff -q .pi/settings.json \"$A/.pi/settings.json\"; diff -q .devin/hooks.v1.json \"$A/.devin/hooks.v1.json\"; diff -q .opencode/package.json \"$A/.opencode/package.json\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"(no output)","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"diff <(node -e \\\"console.log(JSON.stringify(require('./.claude/settings.json')).length)\\\") /dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1; A=/private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/pre-claude; diff -q .claude/settings.json \\\"$A/.claude/settings.json\\\"; diff -q .codex/hooks.json \\\"$A/.codex/hooks.json\\\"; diff -q .pi/settings.json \\\"$A/.pi/settings.json\\\"; diff -q .devin/hooks.v1.json \\\"$A/.devin/hooks.v1.json\\\"; diff -q .opencode/package.json \\\"$A/.opencode/package.json\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524101977,"end":1794524103785}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524114636,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f8b8e5001UQiyTp3ushbzoP","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f8a1f10014vTXIfSfzNkIHQ","type":"tool","id":"call_1931621d20b843058d9ae618","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"user-prompt-submit\\|prompt-advisor\\|advisor\" .devin/hooks.v1.json | head -10; echo \"--- pi refs\"; grep -rn \"prompt-advisor\\|promptAdvisor\" .pi 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -10; echo \"--- pi extension loading doc\"; grep -n \"extensions\" .pi/PLUGINS.md .pi/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -12","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"55:          \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=devin event=UserPromptSubmit adapter=user-prompt-submit.js\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"UserPromptSubmit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk devin hook could not resolve; run npm run build in the spec-kit runtime package\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mkHookDrift\\\\\\\":true}}\\\"; }'\",\n87:          \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && node .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=devin event=PreToolUse adapter=git-preflight-advisory.mjs\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PreToolUse\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mkHookDrift\\\\\\\":true}}\\\"; }'\",\n--- pi refs\n.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts:1:export { default } from '../../.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts';\n.pi/extensions/README.md:32:| `prompt-advisor.ts` | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/` |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:36:Each file is a thin adapter: it registers a handler against one of Pi's lifecycle events (`pi.on(event, handler)`). `goal-context.ts` is the one exception to the adapter shape: it registers a command as well as lifecycle handlers, because Pi is the only runtime here where the goal surface is both an injection and a management command in the same extension. The 15 tool_call/tool_result/input adapters delegate to shared, runtime-neutral core modules under `.skilled/` that the sibling runtimes' bridges under the same concern folders also import, except `prompt-advisor.ts` below. Two of the five session-lifecycle adapters (`session-start-context.ts`, `session-stop-context.ts`) proxy into the Claude lifecycle-hook dist files under `system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/` via `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts` -- the same lifecycle owner devin and cursor already proxy into via their own runtime-specific `spawnSync` adapters, so state and transcript semantics never drift across runtimes. The other three do their own work in-process: `session-start-advisories.ts` runs the repository's own checks through `ctx.exec()`, `session-compact-context.ts` is a native port of the devin post-compaction recovery chain, and `session-relaunch.ts` calls its own shared relaunch core. `prompt-advisor.ts` is the exception: it imports the compiled advisor lifecycle module (`system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`) directly and calls `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit()` in-process, because Pi awaits `input` handlers before agent processing begins and the old two-process `spawnSync` bridge blocked every send. Its visible contribution is lifecycle-deduped: the advisor brief and Pi dispatch reminder render in full on the first message and after `session_start`/`session_compact`, while a proven same-content repeat returns no transform and leaves the raw turn byte-identical (`SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP`, default ON; `0`/`false`/`off` restores always-full). The separate tool-call preflight still enforces dispatch authorization on every turn. Every handler wraps its call in try/catch and fails open: a guard-core or lifecycle-bridge bug must never block or alter work it only observes. `git-message-gate.ts` is the one deliberate blocker beside the dispatch preflight: it returns `{ block: true, reason }` when the shared sk-git gate refuses a commit message, PR description or branch name, and it fails open only when the gate itself cannot load.\n.pi/extensions/README.md:60:+-- prompt-advisor.ts           # Bridges the skill-advisor's UserPromptSubmit recommendation (in-process)\n.pi/extensions/README.md:93:| `prompt-advisor.ts` | `input` | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit()` (in-process dynamic import); full first + boundaries, no transform on proven repeats (`SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP`) |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:124:| Fail-open | Every handler body is wrapped in try/catch. A caught error returns `undefined` (`prompt-advisor.ts`, all others) or `{ action: \"continue\" }` (`spec-gate-classify.ts` only) for `input` handlers, never a block. |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:125:| Output shape | `session-prime.js` writes plain text to stdout. `session-stop.js` writes nothing (side effects only, no top-level stdout emission). `user-prompt-submit.js` writes a `{ hookSpecificOutput: { additionalContext } }` JSON envelope. `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts`'s `extractAdditionalContext()` only applies to the last one. `session-start-context.ts` uses `session-prime.js`'s raw stdout text directly. `prompt-advisor.ts` reads the same envelope from the in-process return value instead of spawned stdout. |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:175:| `promptAdvisor` | Default export | Registers the `input` skill-advisor recommendation bridge. |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:180:| `runClaudeHookAdapter`, `extractAdditionalContext` | Named exports | `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts`'s spawnSync proxy and JSON-envelope parser, imported by the session-lifecycle adapters (session-start/stop); `prompt-advisor.ts` no longer uses it. |\n.pi/extensions/lib/README.md:64:Note: ../prompt-advisor.ts no longer routes through this module -- it\n--- pi extension loading doc\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:8:extensions (`pi-btw`, `pi-plan-build`) install the same way under `git/`;\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:10:extension directories (`.pi/extensions/`). The npm manifests at both scopes\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:82:Local fork at `.pi/extensions/pi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support` — based on [pi-openai-fast-mode](https://github.com/johncmunson/pi-openai-fast-mode) commit `9b28456`\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:117:`pi update --extensions` updates the user scope, but **skips project packages\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:123:cd <repo root with project packages> && pi update --extensions --approve\n.pi/README.md:3:description: \"How the Pi CLI uses this repository: the shared guard cores bridged as TypeScript extensions, generated prompts and agents, the Code Mode server and the checks that confirm the bridges still resolve.\"\n.pi/README.md:7:  - \"pi extensions\"\n.pi/README.md:12:> Pi runs the same guard cores as the other runtimes through TypeScript extensions that re-export adapters kept beside the shared hook code.\n.pi/README.md:23:| **Start with** | Run `pi` in this checkout. Pi loads its extensions when the session starts |\n.pi/README.md:29:Pi has no hook configuration file. Its hooks are TypeScript extensions in `extensions/`, and each one is a one-line file that re-exports the adapter its owning hook core keeps. A fix to a guard therefore reaches Pi without a copy to update.\n.pi/README.md:43:| Hooks and guards | 22 extensions. They cover the advisor, the spec-folder gate, dispatch lint and audit, the task-dispatch guard, the MCP route guard, post-edit quality, the injection screen, the overlay guard, the env-secret guard, completion evidence, decision capture, the ask-surface guard, the sk-git gate and preflight advisory, the session context hooks and the session-relaunch nudge |\n.pi/README.md:53:1. Start Pi from the repository root. It loads `AGENTS.md`, the extensions and the prompt templates.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"55:          \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=devin event=UserPromptSubmit adapter=user-prompt-submit.js\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"UserPromptSubmit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk devin hook could not resolve; run npm run build in the spec-kit runtime package\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mkHookDrift\\\\\\\":true}}\\\"; }'\",\n87:          \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && node .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-preflight-advisory.mjs || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=devin event=PreToolUse adapter=git-preflight-advisory.mjs\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PreToolUse\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mkHookDrift\\\\\\\":true}}\\\"; }'\",\n--- pi refs\n.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts:1:export { default } from '../../.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts';\n.pi/extensions/README.md:32:| `prompt-advisor.ts` | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/` |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:36:Each file is a thin adapter: it registers a handler against one of Pi's lifecycle events (`pi.on(event, handler)`). `goal-context.ts` is the one exception to the adapter shape: it registers a command as well as lifecycle handlers, because Pi is the only runtime here where the goal surface is both an injection and a management command in the same extension. The 15 tool_call/tool_result/input adapters delegate to shared, runtime-neutral core modules under `.skilled/` that the sibling runtimes' bridges under the same concern folders also import, except `prompt-advisor.ts` below. Two of the five session-lifecycle adapters (`session-start-context.ts`, `session-stop-context.ts`) proxy into the Claude lifecycle-hook dist files under `system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/` via `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts` -- the same lifecycle owner devin and cursor already proxy into via their own runtime-specific `spawnSync` adapters, so state and transcript semantics never drift across runtimes. The other three do their own work in-process: `session-start-advisories.ts` runs the repository's own checks through `ctx.exec()`, `session-compact-context.ts` is a native port of the devin post-compaction recovery chain, and `session-relaunch.ts` calls its own shared relaunch core. `prompt-advisor.ts` is the exception: it imports the compiled advisor lifecycle module (`system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`) directly and calls `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit()` in-process, because Pi awaits `input` handlers before agent processing begins and the old two-process `spawnSync` bridge blocked every send. Its visible contribution is lifecycle-deduped: the advisor brief and Pi dispatch reminder render in full on the first message and after `session_start`/`session_compact`, while a proven same-content repeat returns no transform and leaves the raw turn byte-identical (`SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP`, default ON; `0`/`false`/`off` restores always-full). The separate tool-call preflight still enforces dispatch authorization on every turn. Every handler wraps its call in try/catch and fails open: a guard-core or lifecycle-bridge bug must never block or alter work it only observes. `git-message-gate.ts` is the one deliberate blocker beside the dispatch preflight: it returns `{ block: true, reason }` when the shared sk-git gate refuses a commit message, PR description or branch name, and it fails open only when the gate itself cannot load.\n.pi/extensions/README.md:60:+-- prompt-advisor.ts           # Bridges the skill-advisor's UserPromptSubmit recommendation (in-process)\n.pi/extensions/README.md:93:| `prompt-advisor.ts` | `input` | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit()` (in-process dynamic import); full first + boundaries, no transform on proven repeats (`SPECKIT_PI_DIRECTIVE_DEDUP`) |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:124:| Fail-open | Every handler body is wrapped in try/catch. A caught error returns `undefined` (`prompt-advisor.ts`, all others) or `{ action: \"continue\" }` (`spec-gate-classify.ts` only) for `input` handlers, never a block. |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:125:| Output shape | `session-prime.js` writes plain text to stdout. `session-stop.js` writes nothing (side effects only, no top-level stdout emission). `user-prompt-submit.js` writes a `{ hookSpecificOutput: { additionalContext } }` JSON envelope. `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts`'s `extractAdditionalContext()` only applies to the last one. `session-start-context.ts` uses `session-prime.js`'s raw stdout text directly. `prompt-advisor.ts` reads the same envelope from the in-process return value instead of spawned stdout. |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:175:| `promptAdvisor` | Default export | Registers the `input` skill-advisor recommendation bridge. |\n.pi/extensions/README.md:180:| `runClaudeHookAdapter`, `extractAdditionalContext` | Named exports | `lib/claude-hook-adapter.ts`'s spawnSync proxy and JSON-envelope parser, imported by the session-lifecycle adapters (session-start/stop); `prompt-advisor.ts` no longer uses it. |\n.pi/extensions/lib/README.md:64:Note: ../prompt-advisor.ts no longer routes through this module -- it\n--- pi extension loading doc\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:8:extensions (`pi-btw`, `pi-plan-build`) install the same way under `git/`;\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:10:extension directories (`.pi/extensions/`). The npm manifests at both scopes\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:82:Local fork at `.pi/extensions/pi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support` — based on [pi-openai-fast-mode](https://github.com/johncmunson/pi-openai-fast-mode) commit `9b28456`\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:117:`pi update --extensions` updates the user scope, but **skips project packages\n.pi/PLUGINS.md:123:cd <repo root with project packages> && pi update --extensions --approve\n.pi/README.md:3:description: \"How the Pi CLI uses this repository: the shared guard cores bridged as TypeScript extensions, generated prompts and agents, the Code Mode server and the checks that confirm the bridges still resolve.\"\n.pi/README.md:7:  - \"pi extensions\"\n.pi/README.md:12:> Pi runs the same guard cores as the other runtimes through TypeScript extensions that re-export adapters kept beside the shared hook code.\n.pi/README.md:23:| **Start with** | Run `pi` in this checkout. Pi loads its extensions when the session starts |\n.pi/README.md:29:Pi has no hook configuration file. Its hooks are TypeScript extensions in `extensions/`, and each one is a one-line file that re-exports the adapter its owning hook core keeps. A fix to a guard therefore reaches Pi without a copy to update.\n.pi/README.md:43:| Hooks and guards | 22 extensions. They cover the advisor, the spec-folder gate, dispatch lint and audit, the task-dispatch guard, the MCP route guard, post-edit quality, the injection screen, the overlay guard, the env-secret guard, completion evidence, decision capture, the ask-surface guard, the sk-git gate and preflight advisory, the session context hooks and the session-relaunch nudge |\n.pi/README.md:53:1. Start Pi from the repository root. It loads `AGENTS.md`, the extensions and the prompt templates.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"user-prompt-submit\\\\|prompt-advisor\\\\|advisor\\\" .devin/hooks.v1.json | head -10; echo \\\"--- pi refs\\\"; grep -rn \\\"prompt-advisor\\\\|promptAdvisor\\\" .pi 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -10; echo \\\"--- pi extension loading doc\\\"; grep -n \\\"extensions\\\" .pi/PLUGINS.md .pi/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -12\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524100837,"end":1794524114636}}}}
