{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524149091,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f97136001Ib50WLBVNmpvC3","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1f91f23001NFE7p9tX1lJCeJ","type":"tool","id":"call_b5acfe7a0a0840599b1fc9da","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"prompts\\|commands\" .codex/README.md | head -10; echo \"--- opencode commands\"; ls .opencode/commands | head; echo \"--- devin skills\"; ls .devin/skills | head; echo \"--- dsh prompts\"; ls .dsh/prompts | head","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".codex/README.md:3:description: \"How the Codex CLI uses this repository: the agents, prompts and hooks that generators write from .skilled/, how to approve the hooks and how to check that they are in sync.\"\n.codex/README.md:12:> Codex reads this repository through agents, prompts and hooks that generators write from the shared source, so the same guards run in a Codex session.\n.codex/README.md:22:| **Use it for** | Working on this repository in the Codex CLI with the shared agents, prompts and guards |\n.codex/README.md:25:| **Checked by** | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` and the commands in section 5 |\n.codex/README.md:29:Codex cannot read `.skilled/` directly. It wants agents as TOML files, prompts as a flat folder and hooks in its own `hooks.json`. Generators translate the shared source into those formats, and this folder holds their output.\n.codex/README.md:42:| Commands | One prompt stub per command in `prompts/`, written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. A command such as `create/agent` becomes `create-agent`, and the stub tells Codex to read the canonical file in full |\n.codex/README.md:64:| `prompts/*.md` | Generated | Written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. Each stub points at its canonical command file |\n.codex/README.md:79:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs --check\n--- opencode commands\ncreate\ndeep\ndesign\ndoctor\ngoal-opencode.md\nlocal-skilled-alignment.md\nprompt\nREADME.txt\nscripts\nspeckit\n--- devin skills\ncli-classifier\ncli-external-orchestration\ncli-orca\nmcp-code-mode\nmcp-tooling\nREADME.txt\nsk-code\nsk-design\nsk-doc\nsk-git\n--- dsh prompts\ncreate-agent.md\ncreate-benchmark.md\ncreate-changelog.md\ncreate-command.md\ncreate-diff.md\ncreate-feature-catalog.md\ncreate-goal.md\ncreate-manual-testing-playbook.md\ncreate-readme.md\ncreate-repo-rule.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".codex/README.md:3:description: \"How the Codex CLI uses this repository: the agents, prompts and hooks that generators write from .skilled/, how to approve the hooks and how to check that they are in sync.\"\n.codex/README.md:12:> Codex reads this repository through agents, prompts and hooks that generators write from the shared source, so the same guards run in a Codex session.\n.codex/README.md:22:| **Use it for** | Working on this repository in the Codex CLI with the shared agents, prompts and guards |\n.codex/README.md:25:| **Checked by** | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` and the commands in section 5 |\n.codex/README.md:29:Codex cannot read `.skilled/` directly. It wants agents as TOML files, prompts as a flat folder and hooks in its own `hooks.json`. Generators translate the shared source into those formats, and this folder holds their output.\n.codex/README.md:42:| Commands | One prompt stub per command in `prompts/`, written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. A command such as `create/agent` becomes `create-agent`, and the stub tells Codex to read the canonical file in full |\n.codex/README.md:64:| `prompts/*.md` | Generated | Written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. Each stub points at its canonical command file |\n.codex/README.md:79:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs --check\n--- opencode commands\ncreate\ndeep\ndesign\ndoctor\ngoal-o