{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794524190288,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1fa1650001zpMurL43zvGI48","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1fa0d79001lwYAQaoL2oFJvR","type":"step-start","snapshot":"1636e7a4cadd185de29b28b642c37c4b2386d6e7"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524202471,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1fa4176001yNk7MrWQWsvGpf","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1fa0d79001lwYAQaoL2oFJvR","type":"tool","id":"call_0fd93a5fd4e543a9903bb375","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"COMMAND:\\|Command in the brief\\|command registry\\|no command\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md | head -20; echo \"--- tasks 006 bullet\"; grep -n \"Command in the brief\" -A 6 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"521:Correction first: I told you phase 003 (plain-chat command reach) was open only because of its holdout row. That was wrong. It has eight more unmet criteria, and I re-measured them today. Three are still fixable: one typed command (/create:agent) still ties with its own skill, four old spec-kit ids still sit in the Python compatibility list, and the prompt 'show me which packets mention the token cap' still reaches no command. Three are doctor rows whose phrases were reverted, where phase 004 now reaches 3 of 17 tune and 2 of 17 held-out doctor prompts with real embeddings. One is a one-time measurement-order miss. One asks you to judge that the doctor-only phrase gate was widened to every command. I recorded your holdout waiver and left the phase In Progress. How should phase 003 close?\n--- tasks 006 bullet\n54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55:- [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56-- [ ] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on only when the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57-- [ ] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58-- [ ] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59-- [ ] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60-- [ ] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61-- [ ] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n--\n67:- [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68-- [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69-- [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70-- [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71-- [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72-- [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73-- [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n--\n76:- [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77-- [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78-<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"521:Correction first: I told you phase 003 (plain-chat command reach) was open only because of its holdout row. That was wrong. It has eight more unmet criteria, and I re-measured them today. Three are still fixable: one typed command (/create:agent) still ties with its own skill, four old spec-kit ids still sit in the Python compatibility list, and the prompt 'show me which packets mention the token cap' still reaches no command. Three are doctor rows whose phrases were reverted, where phase 004 now reaches 3 of 17 tune and 2 of 17 held-out doctor prompts with real embeddings. One is a one-time measurement-order miss. One asks you to judge that the doctor-only phrase gate was widened to every command. I recorded your holdout waiver and left the phase In Progress. How should phase 003 close?\n--- tasks 006 bullet\n54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55:- [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56-- [ ] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on only when the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57-- [ ] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58-- [ ] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59-- [ ] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60-- [ ] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61-- [ ] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n--\n67:- [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68-- [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69-- [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70-- [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71-- [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72-- [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73-- [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n--\n76:- [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77-- [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78-<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"COMMAND:\\\\|Command in the brief\\\\|command registry\\\\|no command\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md | head -20; echo \\\"--- tasks 006 bullet\\\"; grep -n \\\"Command in the brief\\\" -A 6 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524201334,"end":1794524202471}}}}
