{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524284829,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1fb5135002J1BtD2s3zlI0sd","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d1fb3e5f0015uEYScSMZYh93q","type":"tool","id":"call_8a165fb951a04038936d76fa","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-1794523629654-v541y3\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-1794523629654-v541y3\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-1794523629654-v541y3\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Wiring map, live pre-arm score, and what phases 005-008 already cover\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All six findings are new to this lineage: the pre-arm rate measures spontaneous doc reads, the live log is incomplete, capped runs distort the denominator, DSH is conditionally wired, host command names differ, and G5 is documented but unfixed.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\",\"Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\",\"Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\",\"How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\",\"What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\"],\"answere