{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524606294,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d200699b001glbV8iUMxbR2v3","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d20037ea001OFTIrFGpXa3jNC","type":"tool","id":"call_a4e236a26ce84f1886680ce2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"advisorHookOutcomesPath\\|advisorHookDiagnosticsPath\\|serializeAdvisorHook\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts | head -8; echo \"--- dsh readme\"; grep -n \"promptAdvisor\\|off unless\" .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md | head -6; echo \"--- install doc hooks\"; grep -n \"codex\\|hooks\\|trust\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -12","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"436:export function serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(record: AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord): string {\n450:  await writeBoundedJsonl(path, serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(record), MAX_DURABLE_DIAGNOSTIC_RECORDS);\n487:export function advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n555:export function advisorHookOutcomesPath(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n--- dsh readme\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:120:      promptAdvisor: true\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md:39:| `prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/created`, `session/event`, `agent/pre-step` | Runs the Skill Advisor and adds the brief to the step. Off unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true. | Fails open. |\n--- install doc hooks\n40:Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n75:It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n77:To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n81:The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n100:2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n117:| 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n133:- **Per runtime:** `.claude` with `.mcp.json`, `.opencode`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.pi`.\n331:- [overlay-guard README](.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/README.md): the hook that protects overlay-owned files.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"436:export function serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(record: AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord): string {\n450:  await writeBoundedJsonl(path, serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(record), MAX_DURABLE_DIAGNOSTIC_RECORDS);\n487:export function advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n555:export function advisorHookOutcomesPath(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n--- dsh readme\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:120:      promptAdvisor: true\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md:39:| `prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/created`, `session/event`, `agent/pre-step` | Runs the Skill Advisor and adds the brief to the step. Off unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true. | Fails open. |\n--- install doc hooks\n40:Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n75:It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n77:To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n81:The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n100:2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n117:| 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n133:- **Per runtime:** `.claude` with `.mcp.json`, `.opencode`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.pi`.\n331:- [overlay-guard README](.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/README.md): the hook that protects overlay-owned files.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"advisorHookOutcomesPath\\\\|advisorHookDiagnosticsPath\\\\|serializeAdvisorHook\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts | head -8; echo \\\"--- dsh readme\\\"; grep -n \\\"promptAdvisor\\\\|off unless\\\" .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md | head -6; echo \\\"--- install doc hooks\\\"; grep -n \\\"codex\\\\|hooks\\\\|trust\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -12\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524604827,"end":1794524606294}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794524609487,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"id":"prt_1d2007bcf001QQviHuDtXzTGUC","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d20037ea001OFTIrFGpXa3jNC","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"0419023db4ca6ec2a1d24aba663320fb0476940a","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1192,"output":200,"reasoning":819,"cache":{"read":199936,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794524612053,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"id":"prt_1d20085d5001EzQI05lMVkvqFw","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d2007bd5001k3DOOoKQLMyLwB","type":"step-start","snapshot":"0419023db4ca6ec2a1d24aba663320fb0476940a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524656415,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d200c1cf001VelCe2ReOpSPHh","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d2007bd5001k3DOOoKQLMyLwB","type":"tool","id":"call_e9ab9fce85a24d18ac158e6a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 3: Ranked post-008 changes, and the install steps that decide whether a runtime is reachable at all\n\n## Focus\n\nAnswer Q3: which change after phases 005-008 raises the start rate per runtime, ranked by expected gain for the work, with the exact file and a verification that does not require a full six-runtime arm. Follow the reducer's next focus (the moving pre-arm log) by making the measurement gate explicit rather than treating a snapshot as a baseline.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the install guide's runtime list and the Codex hook-approval contract, then compared them with the runtime table the one-turn runner uses.\n2. Checked the DSH plugin's enabling surface and the doc that names the flag.\n3. Read the advisor brief renderer's options and its existing `runtime` field to test whether a per-runtime head is localized.\n4. Re-read the scorer's aggregation points and the runner's Codex argv to place the measurement changes precisely.\n5. Ranked the candidate changes by expected gain per unit of work using the iteration 1-2 evidence.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Codex surfacing depends on a per-entry approval that the install path never mentions.** Codex runs a project hook only after that exact entry is approved, stored as `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`; the only place this is written down is the repo-internal `.codex/README.md`. `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` tells a new user to build Spec Kit and register Code Mode, and never says to approve hooks. A fresh external repository therefore reaches Codex with no advisor brief, which is the same state the arena is in. [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:40] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:75]\n\n2. **DSH has two independent install blockers, not one.** Its prompt-advisor adapter is off unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true, and `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` lists the supported runtimes as claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi without dsh, so a DSH user is never told to install the surface that carries the flag. The flag's existence is documented only inside the plugin's own README. [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53] [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:120] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:100]\n\n3. **A per-runtime brief head is a small, localized change.** `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions` already carries `readonly runtime?: string`, and the Claude hook already passes its runtime through the lifecycle path; the head simply ignores it. That makes a runtime-specific suffix (the canonical document path for hosts with no command registry) a change inside one function rather than a new data flow. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:48] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:478] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:293]\n\n4. **Pi is the clean test bed for a head change, and the only runtime where it is.** Pi's brief is delivered in the prompt itself (6 of 6 sampled sessions), while Claude injects out of band and Codex is unapproved in the arena. A Pi-only A/B on the six started rows therefore isolates the head change from delivery and trust confounds. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/README.md:93]\n\n5. **Every claimed gain is conditional on two scorer facts that do not exist yet: arm completeness and brief attribution.** The log is still growing (24/24/24/15/13/11 rows at the last check), and the normalized records the scorer reads carry no `Advisor:` line for Claude. A before/after delta without `armComplete` and an offered-command join can be produced by row-set drift or by delivery failure and still look like a model-behaviour change. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1146] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:325]\n\n## Recommendation Set (post-008)\n\nOrdered by expected gain per unit of work. Each names the file, the gain and the check; none repeats a phase 005-008 task.\n\n1. **Report Codex hooks as unapproved, and put the approval step in the install path.**\n   - Files: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (new step after the build), `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/` runtime-mirrors route + `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/` check (report `codex hooks unapproved` when the project has no trusted entry), `.codex/README.md` (link from the install step).\n   - Gain: turns Codex from \"0/12, no brief\" into a measured runtime. The ceiling is the six started rows; the floor is whatever the first approved run shows.\n   - Verify: `rg -n \"approve\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints a hook step; one Codex smoke run's rollout contains `Advisor:`; the doctor route prints `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved` on a fresh clone and `PASS` after approval.\n\n2. **Make the DSH surface visible and on by default in the repo.**\n   - Files: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (add dsh to both runtime lists), `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs` (default `enabled: options.promptAdvisor !== false`), `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md` (update the sentence).\n   - Gain: +1 runtime that can receive a brief at all. Today DSH's start rate is measured under a disabled advisor, so it cannot answer the surfacing question.\n   - Verify: one DSH smoke run's step payload contains `Advisor:`; `rg -c \"dsh\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints at least 2; the plugin test that asserts the off default is updated.\n\n3. **Name the command document in the brief on hosts with no command registry.**\n   - Files: `ADV/lib/render.ts` (use the existing `runtime` option; append `doc .skilled/commands/<ns>/<name>.md` when runtime is codex, pi or dsh), `ADV/tests` golden briefs (three new rows).\n   - Gain: a model that receives the brief no longer has to infer the path from `/create:readme`; Pi is the clean A/B (6 started rows). Expected direction: Pi 0 of 6 started → above 0 on the same rows; the exact number is the measurement.\n   - Verify: a Pi-only A/B on the six started rows with `score-command-transcripts --summary`; `started` rises with no new `unsafe`; the token delta per brief is under the existing cap (`bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`).\n\n4. **Add the measurement gate before any before/after claim.**\n   - Files: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` (`armComplete`, `uncappedStartRate`, `offered`), `run-command-behaviour.mjs` (record the brief hash/offered command in the run line), `ADV/lib/metrics.ts` (add `offeredCommand` to the hook outcome record).\n   - Gain: converts \"start 3 of 12\" into \"offered X of 12, started Y of X, capped Z excluded\", which is the only form in which a delta is evidence.\n   - Verify: a fixture log with 23 of 24 rows prints `arm incomplete`; a fixture with a brief naming `/create:readme` and no doc read prints `offered 1, started 0`.\n\n5. **Reproduce G5, then fix the Claude mirror only if it reproduces.**\n   - Files: a throwaway repo with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=$(mktemp -d)`; if reproduced, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` (Claude-only mirror name for `create/skill.md`) plus the inventory name map from finding 5 in iteration 1.\n   - Gain: 12 hidden `create:*` names become visible on Claude, or the defect is closed as a stand-in artifact. Both outcomes are useful; the current state is an untested claim in a phase doc.\n   - Verify: two listings in one throwaway repo, with and without the `skill.md` basename; the diff names the 12 commands.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises.\"** That is the planned path and cannot be recommended; it is also unverifiable until the two measurement facts exist. The recommendations above are what remains after those phases.\n- **\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief.\"** Unnecessary token cost on Claude and OpenCode, which can resolve the command through their own surfaces; the change is worth it only on hosts with no registry.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- No existing artifact measures a failed host-command invocation (for example a Codex `/create:readme` typed into an exec turn). The scorer sees tool calls and text, not a rejected slash token, so this gap is recorded rather than guessed.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Ambiguous input:** \"raise the start rate\" can mean the product rate or the measured rate. This iteration keeps both and labels which one each recommendation moves.\n- **Contradictory evidence:** none.\n- **Missing dependency:** the exact ceiling for recommendation 3 needs the Pi A/B, which this lineage cannot run (no CLI runs allowed).\n- **Partial success:** the ranking is evidence-based but its top two items are install-path fixes whose gain is bounded by the six started rows, not by all 24.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Q3: Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008? — Answered with the ranked set above: Codex approval + install step, DSH default/install, per-runtime document path, the measurement gate, and the conditional G5 mirror fix.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n1 of 5 in substance: Q4's reproduction and Q5's implementation are now specified but not executed; Q3's ranking needs the Pi A/B to become a number.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`\n- `.codex/README.md`, `.codex/config.toml`, `~/.codex/config.toml`\n- `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `README.md`, `adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts`, `.pi/extensions/README.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`\n- `steer.md`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.7\n- Questions addressed: Q3\n- Questions answered: Q3\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading the install guide as a user would exposed two production blockers (Codex approval, DSH absence) that a repo-internal view hides; the renderer's existing `runtime` option made the head change cheap enough to rank.\n- What did not work and why: no artifact exists for failed host-command invocations, so that path stays a gap.\n- What I would do differently: check the install guide before the runtime shims; it explains why a runtime can be wired in-repo and still unreachable for a user.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 4: the external-repository setup path in detail. Verify how hooks and command mirrors are installed per runtime, whether a fresh repo gets the six surfaces, and what the advisor does when a surface is missing. That closes the install half of the topic with file-level evidence.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 3: Ranked post-008 changes, and the install steps that decide whether a runtime is reachable at all\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAnswer Q3: which change after phases 005-008 raises the start rate per runtime, ranked by expected gain for the work, with the exact file and a verification that does not require a full six-runtime arm. Follow the reducer's next focus (the moving pre-arm log) by making the measurement gate explicit rather than treating a snapshot as a baseline.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the install guide's runtime list and the Codex hook-approval contract, then compared them with the runtime table the one-turn runner uses.\\n2. Checked the DSH plugin's enabling surface and the doc that names the flag.\\n3. Read the advisor brief renderer's options and its existing `runtime` field to test whether a per-runtime head is localized.\\n4. Re-read the scorer's aggregation points and the runner's Codex argv to place the measurement changes precisely.\\n5. Ranked the candidate changes by expected gain per unit of work using the iteration 1-2 evidence.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **Codex surfacing depends on a per-entry approval that the install path never mentions.** Codex runs a project hook only after that exact entry is approved, stored as `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`; the only place this is written down is the repo-internal `.codex/README.md`. `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` tells a new user to build Spec Kit and register Code Mode, and never says to approve hooks. A fresh external repository therefore reaches Codex with no advisor brief, which is the same state the arena is in. [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:40] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:75]\\n\\n2. **DSH has two independent install blockers, not one.** Its prompt-advisor adapter is off unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true, and `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` lists the supported runtimes as claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi without dsh, so a DSH user is never told to install the surface that carries the flag. The flag's existence is documented only inside the plugin's own README. [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53] [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:120] [SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:100]\\n\\n3. **A per-runtime brief head is a small, localized change.** `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions` already carries `readonly runtime?: string`, and the Claude hook already passes its runtime through the lifecycle path; the head simply ignores it. That makes a runtime-specific suffix (the canonical document path for hosts with no command registry) a change inside one function rather than a new data flow. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:48] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:478] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:293]\\n\\n4. **Pi is the clean test bed for a head change, and the only runtime where it is.** Pi's brief is delivered in the prompt itself (6 of 6 sampled sessions), while Claude injects out of band and Codex is unapproved in the arena. A Pi-only A/B on the six started rows therefore isolates the head change from delivery and trust confounds. [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts:1] [SOURCE: .pi/extensions/README.md:93]\\n\\n5. **Every claimed gain is conditional on two scorer facts that do not exist yet: arm completeness and brief attribution.** The log is still growing (24/24/24/15/13/11 rows at the last check), and the normalized records the scorer reads carry no `Advisor:` line for Claude. A before/after delta without `armComplete` and an offered-command join can be produced by row-set drift or by delivery failure and still look like a model-behaviour change. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1146] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:325]\\n\\n## Recommendation Set (post-008)\\n\\nOrdered by expected gain per unit of work. Each names the file, the gain and the check; none repeats a phase 005-008 task.\\n\\n1. **Report Codex hooks as unapproved, and put the approval step in the install path.**\\n   - Files: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (new step after the build), `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/` runtime-mirrors route + `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/` check (report `codex hooks unapproved` when the project has no trusted entry), `.codex/README.md` (link from the install step).\\n   - Gain: turns Codex from \\\"0/12, no brief\\\" into a measured runtime. The ceiling is the six started rows; the floor is whatever the first approved run shows.\\n   - Verify: `rg -n \\\"approve\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints a hook step; one Codex smoke run's rollout contains `Advisor:`; the doctor route prints `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved` on a fresh clone and `PASS` after approval.\\n\\n2. **Make the DSH surface visible and on by default in the repo.**\\n   - Files: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (add dsh to both runtime lists), `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs` (default `enabled: options.promptAdvisor !== false`), `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md` (update the sentence).\\n   - Gain: +1 runtime that can receive a brief at all. Today DSH's start rate is measured under a disabled advisor, so it cannot answer the surfacing question.\\n   - Verify: one DSH smoke run's step payload contains `Advisor:`; `rg -c \\\"dsh\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints at least 2; the plugin test that asserts the off default is updated.\\n\\n3. **Name the command document in the brief on hosts with no command registry.**\\n   - Files: `ADV/lib/render.ts` (use the existing `runtime` option; append `doc .skilled/commands/<ns>/<name>.md` when runtime is codex, pi or dsh), `ADV/tests` golden briefs (three new rows).\\n   - Gain: a model that receives the brief no longer has to infer the path from `/create:readme`; Pi is the clean A/B (6 started rows). Expected direction: Pi 0 of 6 started → above 0 on the same rows; the exact number is the measurement.\\n   - Verify: a Pi-only A/B on the six started rows with `score-command-transcripts --summary`; `started` rises with no new `unsafe`; the token delta per brief is under the existing cap (`bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`).\\n\\n4. **Add the measurement gate before any before/after claim.**\\n   - Files: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` (`armComplete`, `uncappedStartRate`, `offered`), `run-command-behaviour.mjs` (record the brief hash/offered command in the run line), `ADV/lib/metrics.ts` (add `offeredCommand` to the hook outcome record).\\n   - Gain: converts \\\"start 3 of 12\\\" into \\\"offered X of 12, started Y of X, capped Z excluded\\\", which is the only form in which a delta is evidence.\\n   - Verify: a fixture log with 23 of 24 rows prints `arm incomplete`; a fixture with a brief naming `/create:readme` and no doc read prints `offered 1, started 0`.\\n\\n5. **Reproduce G5, then fix the Claude mirror only if it reproduces.**\\n   - Files: a throwaway repo with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=$(mktemp -d)`; if reproduced, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` (Claude-only mirror name for `create/skill.md`) plus the inventory name map from finding 5 in iteration 1.\\n   - Gain: 12 hidden `create:*` names become visible on Claude, or the defect is closed as a stand-in artifact. Both outcomes are useful; the current state is an untested claim in a phase doc.\\n   - Verify: two listings in one throwaway repo, with and without the `skill.md` basename; the diff names the 12 commands.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **\\\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises.\\\"** That is the planned path and cannot be recommended; it is also unverifiable until the two measurement facts exist. The recommendations above are what remains after those phases.\\n- **\\\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief.\\\"** Unnecessary token cost on Claude and OpenCode, which can resolve the command through their own surfaces; the change is worth it only on hosts with no registry.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- No existing artifact measures a failed host-command invocation (for example a Codex `/create:readme` typed into an exec turn). The scorer sees tool calls and text, not a rejected slash token, so this gap is recorded rather than guessed.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Ambiguous input:** \\\"raise the start rate\\\" can mean the product rate or the measured rate. This iteration keeps both and labels which one each recommendation moves.\\n- **Contradictory evidence:** none.\\n- **Missing dependency:** the exact ceiling for recommendation 3 needs the Pi A/B, which this lineage cannot run (no CLI runs allowed).\\n- **Partial success:** the ranking is evidence-based but its top two items are install-path fixes whose gain is bounded by the six started rows, not by all 24.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Q3: Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008? — Answered with the ranked set above: Codex approval + install step, DSH default/install, per-runtime document path, the measurement gate, and the conditional G5 mirror fix.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n1 of 5 in substance: Q4's reproduction and Q5's implementation are now specified but not executed; Q3's ranking needs the Pi A/B to become a number.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`\\n- `.codex/README.md`, `.codex/config.toml`, `~/.codex/config.toml`\\n- `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`, `README.md`, `adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts`, `.pi/extensions/README.md`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`\\n- `steer.md`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.7\\n- Questions addressed: Q3\\n- Questions answered: Q3\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: reading the install guide as a user would exposed two production blockers (Codex approval, DSH absence) that a repo-internal view hides; the renderer's existing `runtime` option made the head change cheap enough to rank.\\n- What did not work and why: no artifact exists for failed host-command invocations, so that path stays a gap.\\n- What I would do differently: check the install guide before the runtime shims; it explains why a runtime can be wired in-repo and still unreachable for a user.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nIteration 4: the external-repository setup path in detail. Verify how hooks and command mirrors are installed per runtime, whether a fresh repo gets the six surfaces, and what the advisor does when a surface is missing. That closes the install half of the topic with file-level evidence.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524627407,"end":1794524656415}}}}
