{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524675171,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d201558f001MI4MfUCGYpI7dO","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O","messageID":"msg_1d2014f09001z5ZXI34SkPsY2b","type":"tool","id":"call_e6b20a182d7445daa0f741de","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"runId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-1794523629654-v541y3\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-1794523629654-v541y3\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-1794523629654-v541y3\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Ranked post-008 changes, and the install steps that decide whether a runtime is reachable at all\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.7,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Two findings are fully new (the Codex approval gap in the install path and the renderer's unused runtime option), two partially new (DSH install absence, measurement gate), and one synthesis (Pi as the clean test bed).\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\",\"Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\",\"Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\",\"How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\",\"What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises\",\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief\"],\"focusTrack\":\"cross-cli\",\"edgeCase\":\"missing-dependency\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Bash\",\"Read\",\"Grep\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\".codex/README.md\",\".codex/config.toml\",\"~/.codex/config.toml\",\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\",\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\",\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts\",\".pi/extensions/README.md\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl\",\"steer.md\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T23:04:22.000Z\",\"durationMs\":120000}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-001\",\"label\":\"Codex surfacing depends on a manual per-entry hook approval stored in ~/.codex/config.toml, and INSTALL-SKILLED.md never mentions it, so a fresh external repo reaches Codex with no advisor brief.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".codex/README.md\",\"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-002\",\"label\":\"DSH has two independent install blockers: its prompt-advisor defaults off without a repo config, and INSTALL-SKILLED.md omits dsh from both runtime lists.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\",\".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\",\"INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-003\",\"label\":\"A per-runtime brief head is localized: AdvisorBriefRenderOptions already carries runtime, the Claude hook already passes it, and only renderAdvisorBrief ignores it.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-004\",\"label\":\"Pi is the only runtime where a brief-head A/B is clean, because its brief is in-prompt in 6 of 6 sampled sessions while Claude injects out of band and Codex is unapproved in the arena.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts\",\".pi/extensions/README.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-005\",\"label\":\"Every claimed start-rate gain is conditional on arm completeness and brief attribution, neither of which the scorer reports today while the pre-arm log keeps growing.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises\",\"reason\":\"Planned work cannot be re-recommended, and it is unverifiable until arm completeness and brief attribution exist.\",\"iteration\":3}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief\",\"reason\":\"Claude and OpenCode resolve commands through their own surfaces, so the path only pays on hosts with no registry.\",\"iteration\":3}\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deltas/iter-003.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-rese